=[sisho-tui]

Shared Ratatui chrome, theme, and modal primitives for `sisho` TUI tools.

This crate provides a minimal, consistent visual shell across `sisho` terminal
interfaces without coupling to any application state or event loop:

- `theme`: \[`Theme`\] palette and reusable pane/tab/keybinding styles.
- `shell`: \[`ShellLayout`\] standard header/body/footer vertical split.
- `header`: \[`HeaderBar`\] and \[`TabItem`\] top bar with optional context and badges.
- `footer`: \[`FooterBar`\], \[`KeyHint`\], \[`StatusLine`\], and \[`StatusKind`\] two-line footer.
- `modal`: \[`centered_rect`\], \[`ModalFrame`\], \[`HelpSection`\], \[`HelpRow`\], and \[`draw_help_modal`\].

==[Module footer]

Two-line bottom footer bar showing key hints and status or summary text.

===[Structs]

====[struct StatusLine]

Status message displayed on the second line of \[`FooterBar`\].

====[struct KeyHint]

A single keybinding hint rendered on the first line of \[`FooterBar`\].

====[struct FooterBar]

Two-line footer widget rendering keybinding hints above a status or summary line.

===[Enums]

====[enum StatusKind]

Severity level for a footer status message.

==[Module header]

Top header bar widget with application name, optional context, and tab strip.

===[Structs]

====[struct TabItem]

A single selectable view tab rendered inside \[`HeaderBar`\].

====[struct HeaderBar]

Top chrome bar displaying the application title, optional context, and view tabs.

==[Module modal]

Centered modal dialog frame and structured keybinding help overlay.

===[Structs]

====[struct ModalFrame]

Centered, bordered modal container that clears its background and returns its inner area.

====[struct HelpRow]

A single keybinding entry inside a \[`HelpSection`\].

====[struct HelpSection]

A titled group of \[`HelpRow`\] items rendered inside \[`draw_help_modal`\].

===[Functions]

====[fn centered_rect]

Computes a centered rectangle occupying `percent_x` by `percent_y` of `area`.

Percentages above `100` are clamped to `100`.

====[fn draw_help_modal]

Renders a centered keybinding help overlay from `sections` and an optional `footer_hint`.

==[Module shell]

Top-level vertical layout splitting a screen into header, body, and footer regions.

===[Structs]

====[struct ShellLayout]

Standard three-row chrome layout shared by `sisho` TUI screens.

==[Module theme]

Color palette and widget styling primitives for `sisho` TUI applications.

===[Structs]

====[struct Theme]

Color palette and reusable widget styles shared across `sisho` TUI tools.
